  "item": "R1",
  "scores": {"U": 2, "A": 2, "C": 3, "V": 1},
  "confidences": {"U": 0.9, "A": 0.95, "C": 0.8, "V": 0.95},
  "rationales": {"U":"'optional features' and 'shall then be implemented as specified in the EIRENE FRS and SRS' lack contextual definition — readers cannot determine which features are optional, what 'then' conditions trigger implementation, or whether 'FRS and SRS' refer to current versions; this violates atomicity and traceability for stakeholders unfamiliar with internal document naming conventions","A":"'optional features' is inherently ambiguous — no enumeration, exclusion criteria, or scope boundary is provided; 'shall then be implemented' introduces temporal and conditional vagueness without defining the triggering event or applicability context","C":"The statement is likely correct as a policy-level assertion but lacks technical precision — it defers correctness to external documents without verifying their existence, consistency, or version alignment; however, no internal contradiction is evident, so score is moderate","V":"No testable criterion is present — 'may include', 'optional', and reference to unspecified external documents ('FRS and SRS') make it impossible to design a pass/fail verification procedure; no measurable behavior, input, output, or constraint is stated"},
  "suggestions": {"U":"Replace with an explicit, bounded list of optional features (e.g., 'EIRENE network optional features: X, Y, Z'), each linked to a unique identifier and defined in Section N of this specification","A":"Replace with 'The EIRENE network shall support zero or more of the following optional features: Feature-X (ID: OPT-001), Feature-Y (ID: OPT-002), Feature-Z (ID: OPT-003); if any is selected, its implementation shall conform to the requirements in Table 4.2 and Sections 5.1–5.3 of this specification'","C":"Keep unchanged — the deference to FRS/SRS is acceptable for high-level allocation, provided those documents are formally controlled and referenced by version; however, add '(v2.1, dated 2024-03-15)' after 'EIRENE FRS and SRS' to anchor correctness","V":"Replace with 'For each optional feature selected in the deployment configuration, the EIRENE network shall exhibit behavior B1 when input I1 is applied, produce output O1 within t1 ms, and satisfy constraint C1 (see Table 4.2); absence of selection shall result in no instantiation of that feature’s runtime components'"},
